Change Page Profile Photo.code:
// Change a Facebook Page's profile picture.
// Limitation: the facebook adaptor only wraps the Messenger Send API (POST /me/messages).
// It can't update Page settings or the profile picture; do that in a separate step with the
// http adaptor against the Graph API, using a Page access token with pages_manage_metadata.
// The closest thing this adaptor can do is send the new image to someone over Messenger:
postMessage({
  recipient: { id: $.data.psid },
  message: {
    attachment: { type: 'image', payload: { url: $.data.photoUrl, is_reusable: true } },
  },
});

Create Page Photo.code:
// Share a photo from your Page.
// Limitation: the facebook adaptor only wraps the Messenger Send API (POST /me/messages).
// It can't publish to the Page feed; instead it sends the photo to a person (PSID) over Messenger.
postMessage({
  recipient: { id: $.data.psid },
  message: {
    attachment: {
      type: 'image',
      // Publicly reachable image URL.
      payload: { url: $.data.photoUrl, is_reusable: true },
    },
  },
});

Create Page Post.code:
// Post a message to your Facebook Page feed.
// The postMessage helper wraps the Graph API /{page-id}/feed endpoint.
postMessage({
  recipient: { id: $.configuration.pageId },
  message: {
    text: `New update from OpenFn: ${$.data.summary}`,
  },
});

